      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "To a stirred solution of allyl-modified benzimidazole ligand HL (0.4 mmol, 0.112 g) in absolute MeOH (15 ml) was added Ln(NO3)3·6H2O (0.4 mmol; for La, 0.173 g) in absolute MeOH (5 ml). The mixture was refluxed under N2 for 6 h, cooled to room temperature, filtered, and diethyl ether was allowed to diffuse into the pale yellow filtrate at room temperature. Pale yellow microcrystalline 1 was obtained in about two weeks.",
